A||||6||Turbo88||RAM kevlar racing clutch from the Fiero Store||||1||
Z||000000||Turbo88||10-21-2001||11:05 PM||||Just an FYI to everyone and you searching people out there...<P>The RAM Racing Clutch on the Fiero Store's website didn't fit right on my car. The splined hub has a protrusion that sticks out from the center. That protruding section rubs firmly against the thrust bearing's bushing. When I installed the clutch I heard this terrible squeal from that area so I decided to tear it all back apart and take a look. It got hot enough to melt the end of that bushing and form a nice little lip. I used my handly Dremel tool and took about 1/4 of an inch off that protusion and cleaned the lip off of the T/O bushing. Slapped it all back together and it works like a champ. I test fitted the clutch both ways just to be sure and it would have rubbed against the center of the crankshaft if installed the other way. RAM recommends installing it with the protrusion facing into the trans as I had originally installed it.<P>The clutch has so little pressure but when you release it had, it grabs like a clamp! I'm impressed with the clutch other than the above..<P>I contacted RAM and the Fiero Store with questions and both were extremely helpful. I have sent this problem to both and feel confident it will be addressed. <P>-Bryan||||reg||1
Z||000001||SLYGUY||10-22-2001||01:50 AM||||Glad to hear that you got that fixed.<BR>The throwout bearing on my 88GT is on it's way out so I'm looking at a clutch job soon. <BR>How difficult was it for you to do? You didn't have to remove the engine/tranny or cradle?<BR>Being able to do it myself would save me about $700!!!<BR>How did you do it?<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ViewImage.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Turbo88||10-22-2001||10:06 AM||||Well, I would say first to prepare yourself for busted up hands! Beyond that, it's easy. In a weekend (last weekend) I pulled out the engine cradle, removed my clutch, modified it, put it back together, changed the fuel pump relay, removed the fuel tank, changed the fuel pump and strainer, flushed the cooling system and put fresh antifreeze in, and about 1000 random fixes including plugs, PVC, net battery, ect. <P>It actually looks much harder than it is in my opinion. Just remember a couple peices of advice. Put a floor jack under the engine cradle and take out the two rear bolts. Use the floor jack to lower the rear of the engine cradle and you can access everything you need on the front of the engine. The AC compressor is a pain. Also, if you have a Haynes manual, it will be all but useless for this. It tells you to disconnect all the sensor's wiring but DO NOT do that. Next to the battery is a large connector. Unbolt that. Remove your ECM and disconnect the wiring harness from it and feed it back through the firewall. Be prepared to have antifreeze all over you and lots of dust/sand/small rocks drop into your eyes. Have a willing partner aswell. <P>I recommend having two 18mm wrenches and an 18mm impact socket (I broke two sockets before I went up to the store to get them replaced about bought an impact socket). Have 15, 13, and 10mm shallow and deep sockets. These are the most common tools I used but there were some odds and ends. You can have the car off the cradle in a 1/2 day if you have a good assortment of hand tools and a vehicle host (or two large floor jacks). <P>Good luck with it!! Feel free to write if you have any questions..<P>-Bryan<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||10-22-2001||11:14 PM||||A set of (metric) GearWrenches (NAPA has them) and a 3/8" air-ratchet with impact sockets!!!<P>I couldn't imagine doing it withought these tools.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||DreXteR||10-23-2001||01:16 PM||||How much power it handles??<P>DreX<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/fierofire1.jpg">        <BR>  <BR>Just another Red Fiero - Back 2 the Future Prototype. :D||||reg||1
